      "id": 1,
      "text": "Goodyears Bar was founded in 1849 when brothers Miles and Andrew Goodyear discovered gold, giving the town its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goodyears_Bar%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town once hosted 3,000 to 5,000 residents and 51 businesses, making it a bustling gold rush hub before the 1864 fire.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://sierracountychamber.com/Goodyears-Bar"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 1864 stage stop, now the Helm's St., survives as a historic building, showing the town’s early transportation role.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://sierracountychamber.com/Goodyears-Bar"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Goodyears Bar Schoolhouse, built around 1872, still serves the community and now houses a museum with four exhibits on Sierra County history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://sierracountychamber.com/Goodyears-Bar"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Folk singer Kate Wolf is buried in Goodyears Bar, linking the town to a notable cultural figure.",
